One way to stop him from stealing your stuff is to drop the stuff he
steals in a level you don't tend to visit too often, such as the lowest
level you have found. I'd still hang on to the bow, especially if you 
have lots of good arrows. If you don't have them, I think you should
make them. 

Unfortunately this will not stop him from reappearing, but it should make
his reappearances last a bit shorter.

> Also, someone keeps zapping me with a spell of
> "malignant aura", and my stuff keeps getting cursed,
> and I'm running out of holy water to uncurse it with.

Apart from curses from monsters, there are only two ways to improve on 
this that I can think of, and neither of them grants you total protection.

The more inefficient way is to add useless items to your inventory until
it's full, so that a larger portion of the curses land on items you don't
need to be uncursed. The more effective way is to wield Magicbane, but 
even that isn't proof against all curses.

> How does one fight back against "curse and/or unbless
> your stuff" attacks?

What I do before the phase of the game where I'm subject to random cursing 
of items is to make sure that I need to spend very little time at that 
phase. So in this respect you are unfortunately somewhat too late in 
this game.

And I keep a stock of ways to uncurse things that need to be uncursed and
to bless things that I prefer to be blessed. Some things work just as well
whether they are cursed, uncursed, or blessed. For blessing my
all-too-heavy bag of holding, I keep some holy water in another bag that
works just as well if it gets cursed.

